# Scoped external-service tokens, injected at runtime (never baked into image).
# Copy to .env and fill. .env is gitignored.
#
# Each token should be the narrowest scope the agent needs. Readonly where possible.

# LiteLLM proxy key — referenced by pi-config/agent/models.json as $LITELLM_API_KEY.
# LITELLM_API_KEY=

# GitHub PAT. Not used here: put it in ~/.tau/secrets/git.env and gh.env, which
# only the git and gh proxies read. Scope decides the agent's GitHub reach: contents:write + pull_requests:write
# on selected repos lets it push branches and open PRs; branch protection on
# the repos is the merge gate.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Linear API key — read natively by the `linear` CLI (schpet/linear-cli) as LINEAR_API_KEY. Create one at linear.app/settings/account/security. Readonly
# where the agent only needs to read issues.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=

# Slack user token (xoxp-) - read by the `slack` CLI as
# SLACK_USER_TOKEN. The agent acts as you: `slack api chat.postMessage channel=C0123
# text=hi`. Needs user scopes for what it should do, e.g. channels:read groups:read
# users:read channels:history groups:history chat:write. Leave SLACK_BOT_TOKEN unset:
# the CLI prefers it over the user token and would act as the app instead.
# SLACK_USER_TOKEN=

# DATADOG_API_KEY=
# SOME_SERVICE_TOKEN=
